Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:08:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Mark both coincident stars when a chart dot is poked
 (E3/E5, O1/O7)

Letters that revisit a point (E and O in the title; B, D, Q, Y too)
generate two coincident star spheres there under different names, but
the Star Chart shows one dot per point named after the first star. Only
that star was marked, so its unmarked twin hid the mark: in the sky the
twin's SkyStarTwinkle glow (3.5x size, whitish core, additive) washed
the yellow out since ec2b884; on the wooden mini the two spheres
depth-fight.

ConstellationSetup.BuildStarLookup now maps every name at a shared
point to all the generated stars there (mini and sky), using
ConstellationStarKeys.PositionKey, the same rounded affinity-px key
StarChartLayout uses for its dots. Marking and unmarking go through the
same list, so nothing stays marked. Star generation, the chart, the
materials and the scene are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
